## 2. The decided rule

### [CXC-SCL-HOST-CITES-VERSION] Rule 1: a host-side change cites the contract version it implements

- rule: "a host-side change cites the contract version it implements."
- applies-to: every ComposeIO host-side change and, by the same standing order, Gnomon's GM-SPEC-CHECKLIST (which gains the same rule; that file is not edited here).
- verify-machine: each host-side change record (spec revision, commit message or decision node) names one `plugin-contract-vX.Y` tag, and a check over the change set finds no host-side change without it.
- status: decided
- status-detail: decided — Plumb's addendum, accepted by the architect
- provenance: Plumb's addendum to the brief, accepted by the architect (2026-11-26); see [CXC-PC-STANDING-HOST-CITES-VERSION].
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-SPEC-CHECKLIST]
- see-also: [CXC-PC-STANDING-HOST-CITES-VERSION], [CXC-PC-VERSION-RULE], [CXC-PC-RELEASE-TAGS]

---

